LONG.update({
'muslim-wedding-album-design':('Designing a Muslim Wedding Album: Layout Ideas',[
"Muslim weddings in India are usually planned around a few key moments, most often the Nikah, family portraits and the Walima reception, with other functions such as mehendi or haldi depending on family and region. Designing the album around these moments, and around the family's preferences, makes the book feel personal and respectful.",
"## Understand the family's preferences first",
"Customs vary widely between communities and families. Before design, ask which events the couple wants included, whether some photos should be kept private or left out, and whether the family prefers more family portraits or more couple images. Some families prefer modest layouts with fewer close couple shots in the main album; others want a modern, editorial style. Planning this in advance avoids uncomfortable redesigns.",
"## Suggested album structure",
"- Opening spread with the couple's names and date.",
"- Preparations and mehendi, if photographed.",
"- The Nikah: arrivals, the ceremony, signing, duas and blessings.",
"- Family portraits from both sides, with clear group spreads.",
"- Couple portraits.",
"- The Walima reception: entry, stage, guests and celebration.",
"- Details: decor, invitation, jewellery and food.",
"- Closing spread.",
"## Design motifs that suit Muslim albums",
"Geometric patterns, arches, lanterns, soft gold, emerald and ivory are popular choices. Use these motifs as frames and accents rather than covering whole pages. Many templates in our [Muslim wedding album PSD collection](/muslim-wedding-album-psd/) use arches and geometric borders that work well around portraits.",
"## Calligraphy and text",
"Some couples like Arabic or Urdu calligraphy, a short verse or a blessing on the opening page. Use correct text supplied or approved by the family; never copy calligraphy you cannot read and verify. Keep calligraphy as a design element on its own space, not overlapping faces. For English text, a clean serif or a refined script pairs well with geometric motifs.",
"## Colour themes",
"Take the palette from the outfits and decor. Deep green, maroon, gold and ivory are classic combinations, while pastel mint, blush and champagne suit modern weddings. Keep the palette consistent across events, changing only slightly between the Nikah and the Walima.",
"## Layout tips",
"- Give the Nikah moments clean, uncluttered spreads with large photos.",
"- Use sequence strips for the signing and blessings.",
"- Plan family group spreads carefully and label them if the family wants names included.",
"- Keep faces away from the centre fold and inside the safe area.",
"## Practical workflow",
"Organise photos in event order, correct colour per lighting group and make a page plan for client approval before designing. Our guides on [organising photos](/blog/organise-photos-before-album-design/) and [editing a wedding album PSD](/blog/how-to-edit-wedding-album-psd/) cover these steps.",
"## Covers",
"A simple cover with one elegant couple portrait or a decorative geometric design with names works best. If the family prefers, a cover without a photo, using only names, a date and a pattern, is a classic option. See the [album cover PSD collection](/album-cover-psd/) for front panel layouts.",
"A Muslim wedding album succeeds when it reflects the family's own customs and comfort level. Ask, plan, and let the photos of the Nikah and the families carry the album."]),
'christian-wedding-album-design':('Christian Wedding Album Layout Ideas',[
"Christian weddings in India combine church ceremonies with family traditions that vary by region and denomination, from Kerala and Goa to Tamil Nadu and the North East. A good album follows the order of the day and balances the solemn church service with the joyful reception.",
"## Typical album structure",
"- Opening spread with the couple's portrait, names and date.",
"- Bride's and groom's preparations: dress, veil, flowers, family blessings.",
"- Arrival at the church.",
"- The ceremony: the bride's entry, readings, exchange of vows and rings, the blessing and signing of the register.",
"- Exiting the church and confetti or flower moments.",
"- Couple portraits.",
"- Family and friends group photos.",
"- Reception: entry, cake cutting, toasts, first dance, games.",
"- Details and a closing spread.",
"Ask the couple which moments matter most; customs such as the minnu or manthrakodi in Kerala Christian weddings deserve their own photos and possibly their own spread.",
"## Design style",
"Christian wedding albums often suit white, ivory, champagne, blush and soft gold palettes, with floral or lace details. Elegant serif or script typography for names works well. Keep church interiors clean in the layout; the architecture and light are already strong visual elements, so heavy ornaments are rarely needed.",
"## Ceremony spreads",
"Use wide frames for the church interior and the bride's walk down the aisle, and sequence strips for the vows and ring exchange. The signing of the register and the blessing make good supporting photos. Avoid crowding these spreads; give the important moments space.",
"## Reception spreads",
"Receptions are more energetic. Use more frames, candid images of dancing and toasts, and a sequence for the cake cutting. Keep the same fonts and colours as the ceremony section so the album remains consistent.",
"## Text and verses",
"Some couples like a short Bible verse or a meaningful line on the opening or closing spread. Use the exact text and version the couple provides and proofread it carefully.",
"## Lighting challenges",
"Church interiors can mix daylight from windows with warm artificial light. Correct white balance carefully so the bride's white gown looks clean rather than yellow or blue, and keep detail in the gown's highlights. Our [colour correction tips](/blog/album-colour-correction-tips/) cover mixed lighting.",
"## Templates",
"Choose clean, elegant layouts with floral or minimal decoration from the [Christian wedding album PSD tag](/tag/christian-wedding-album-psd/) or the broader [wedding album design PSD collection](/wedding-album-design-psd/). Many floral and pastel templates suit Christian weddings once you recolour the ornaments to the couple's palette with a clipped Hue/Saturation layer.",
"## Final checks",
"Confirm names, the date, the church name and any verse text with the couple in writing. Keep text and faces away from the centre fold, export in sRGB and run the [print-ready checklist](/blog/print-ready-psd-checklist/) before sending files to the lab."]),
'hindu-wedding-album-design':('Hindu Wedding Album Design Tips',[
"Hindu weddings in India span many regional traditions, with multiple ceremonies spread over one or several days. A good album organises this richness into a clear story, gives the most meaningful rituals space and keeps the design consistent from the first ceremony to the reception.",
"## Map the ceremonies first",
"Ask the family for the list and order of ceremonies, because they differ by region and community. A North Indian wedding may include haldi, mehendi, sangeet, baraat, jaimala, pheras and vidaai; a Tamil wedding may include nichayathartham, the muhurtham, oonjal and saptapadi; Telugu and Kerala weddings have their own sequences. Write the order down and use it as the backbone of the album. Our [Tamil wedding album page order](/blog/tamil-wedding-album-page-order/) is one example.",
"## Give key rituals their own spreads",
"The moments families value most are usually the central rituals: the thali or mangalsutra tying, the pheras or saptapadi, kanyadaan, and blessings from elders. Use large frames and sequence strips for these, and avoid crowding them with unrelated photos.",
"## Colour and motifs",
"Red, maroon, gold, saffron and deep green are traditional colours, while many modern couples prefer pastels for mehendi and haldi. Temple architecture, diyas, marigolds, mandala and paisley patterns are common motifs. Use them as frames and accents; heavy decoration behind faces makes spreads look busy. The [Tamil](/tamil-wedding-album-psd/), [Telugu](/telugu-wedding-album-psd/) and [Kerala](/kerala-wedding-album-psd/) collections show regional styles.",
"## Different moods for different events",
"- **Haldi and mehendi:** bright, playful layouts with candid photos.",
"- **Sangeet:** energetic spreads with dance and performance images.",
"- **Main ceremony:** classic, balanced layouts with fewer, larger photos.",
"- **Reception:** glamorous stage and portrait spreads.",
"Keep the same font pair and a related colour palette across all events so the album still reads as one book.",
"## Family spreads",
"Hindu weddings involve large extended families. Plan dedicated family group spreads for both sides, agree on the must-include groups in advance and check that nobody important is missing before printing.",
"## Text",
"Event titles in English or in the family's language add structure. Use correct Unicode fonts for Indian scripts and ask a fluent person to proofread. A short shloka or blessing on the opening spread is a nice touch when provided by the family.",
"## Practical tips",
"- Ritual photos are often taken under mixed light near the fire or mandap; correct skin tones carefully.",
"- Keep the thali tying and similar close moments away from the centre fold.",
"- Use one template family per event and recolour ornaments to match.",
"- Get client approval on a preview PDF before printing.",
"## Templates",
"Browse the [Indian wedding album PSD tag](/tag/indian-wedding-album-psd/) and the [Karizma album collection](/karizma-album-psd/) for traditional layouts at 12x36, then follow the [layout rules](/blog/wedding-album-layout-rules/) to adapt them to your photos."]),
'pre-wedding-album-ideas':('Pre-Wedding Album Design Ideas',[
"Pre-wedding shoots are more cinematic, personal and relaxed than wedding-day coverage, so their albums need a different design approach. Clean layouts, bigger photos and a clear mood usually work better than heavily decorated traditional templates.",
"## Choose the right size",
"Pre-wedding albums are often shorter than the main wedding album and work well in 12x24 square or 12x36 panoramic formats. A 12x18 compact album is a good choice for a gift or a smaller package. Our [12x18 album PSD collection](/12x18-album-psd/) and [pre-wedding album PSDs](/pre-wedding-album-psd/) include suitable layouts.",
"## Let the photos breathe",
"Pre-wedding photos are usually composed as standalone images: wide landscapes, close portraits, silhouettes at sunset. Give them space. Many spreads can carry a single full-width image or two images with generous margins. Avoid filling pages with small frames.",
"## Build a story",
"Even a short album benefits from structure. Common approaches are:",
"- By location: beach, heritage site, city streets, studio.",
"- By outfit: each change of outfit becomes a small chapter.",
"- By time of day: morning light, golden hour, night.",
"- By the couple's story: how they met, the proposal, the shoot.",
"## Typography and text",
"Pre-wedding albums suit modern typography: clean sans-serif fonts, elegant serif headings or a single refined script for names. Short captions, a date or a meaningful line can add personality. Keep text minimal and away from faces.",
"## Colour grading consistency",
"Pre-wedding shoots often have a deliberate colour grade: warm film-like tones, cool moody tones or bright and airy. Keep the grade consistent throughout the album and choose backgrounds and ornaments that match it. Mixing heavily graded photos with very saturated templates looks inconsistent.",
"## Layout ideas",
"- **Panoramic hero:** one landscape image across the whole spread.",
"- **Diptych:** two portraits side by side with a thin gutter.",
"- **Film strip:** a row of three to five frames showing movement.",
"- **Quote page:** a single photo on one side, short text on the other.",
"- **Detail page:** close-ups of hands, rings and outfits.",
"## Mind the fold",
"Panoramic photos look great across a spread, but make sure faces are not on the fold. Position the couple on the left or right third of the image.",
"## Combine with the wedding album",
"Some couples prefer the pre-wedding section at the beginning of the main wedding album; others want a separate album. If combined, use a different but related design style for the pre-wedding section so the transition to traditional wedding spreads feels intentional.",
"## Getting started",
"Pick a clean template from the [pre-wedding album PSD collection](/pre-wedding-album-psd/), hide decorative elements that do not match the photos, and follow our guide on [editing a wedding album PSD](/blog/how-to-edit-wedding-album-psd/) for the technical steps."]),
'engagement-album-layouts':('Engagement Album Layout Ideas',[
"An engagement or ring ceremony is often the first formal event of an Indian wedding, and many families order a separate engagement album or a dedicated section in the main album. The design should give the ring exchange and the couple centre stage, while including family blessings and the celebration.",
"## Typical structure",
"- Opening spread: couple portrait with names and the engagement date.",
"- Preparations and arrivals.",
"- Ceremony rituals, which vary by community (for example nichayathartham in Tamil weddings or the ring ceremony and roka in North Indian weddings).",
"- The ring exchange in sequence.",
"- Blessings from elders.",
"- Couple portraits.",
"- Family groups.",
"- Celebration, dinner and guests.",
"- Closing spread.",
"## The ring exchange spread",
"Plan a spread specifically for the ring exchange. A sequence strip of three to five frames shows the moment unfolding, while one large close-up of the rings on hands works as the hero. Keep this spread clean, with minimal ornaments.",
"## Size and length",
"Engagement albums are usually shorter than wedding albums. Smaller formats such as 12x30 or 12x24 keep costs reasonable. If the engagement forms a section of the main album, keep it to a few sheets so it does not overshadow the wedding day.",
"## Design style",
"Engagements are often more relaxed than the wedding itself, so lighter, brighter designs work well: pastel backgrounds, floral accents and modern typography. Match the palette to the couple's outfits and the venue decor. Our [engagement album PSD collection](/engagement-album-psd/) includes layouts designed around ring and couple photos.",
"## Couple portraits",
"Engagement shoots often include the first formal portraits of the couple together. Give them at least one minimal spread with large photos, similar to a pre-wedding style. See [pre-wedding album design ideas](/blog/pre-wedding-album-ideas/) for layout inspiration.",
"## Family and guest photos",
"Families value photos with elders and relatives. Plan a family spread and a guest spread rather than scattering group photos throughout. Check with the family which groups must appear.",
"## Text",
"Names, the date and a short line such as 'The beginning of forever' are common, but keep it tasteful and approved by the couple. Use the same font pair throughout the album.",
"## Technical reminders",
"- Rings and hands are small details; use your sharpest images and avoid enlarging crops beyond their resolution.",
"- Keep faces and rings away from the centre fold.",
"- Correct colour carefully; engagement venues often mix stage lights and daylight.",
"- Get client approval on all spreads before printing.",
"## Linking to the wedding album",
"If the same studio designs the wedding album, use a related style so both albums look like a set. A matching cover design with the same typography makes a strong impression when the two albums sit side by side. Explore the [album cover PSD collection](/album-cover-psd/) for matching cover layouts."]),
'kerala-wedding-album-design-ideas':('Kerala Wedding Album Design Ideas',[
"Kerala weddings are known for their elegance: kasavu sarees in cream and gold, jasmine flowers, temple or church settings and relatively short, focused ceremonies. Albums that reflect this restraint, with clean layouts and plenty of space, tend to look best.",
"## Colour palette",
"Cream, off-white, gold and soft green are the classic Kerala palette, drawn from kasavu fabric, jasmine and the greenery of the state. Deep maroon or temple red can appear as an accent. Avoid very saturated, busy templates; they clash with the understated style of most Kerala weddings.",
"## Hindu Kerala weddings",
"Hindu weddings in Kerala are often held at temples or auditoriums and can be relatively brief. Key moments typically include the bride's arrival, the thali tying, the exchange of garlands and the pudava ceremony. Because the main ceremony is short, give these moments large frames and clear sequence spreads. Ask the family about the exact customs, which vary by community.",
"## Christian and Muslim Kerala weddings",
"Kerala Christian weddings may include the minnu kettu and the manthrakodi, along with a church ceremony. Muslim weddings in Kerala have their own customs. Adapt the album structure to the ceremony and ask the family which moments are most important. See our guides on [Christian](/blog/christian-wedding-album-design/) and [Muslim wedding album design](/blog/muslim-wedding-album-design/).",
"## Layout ideas",
"- **Minimal hero spreads:** one large portrait in kasavu and gold on a cream background.",
"- **Detail spreads:** jasmine, gold jewellery, the thali or minnu, the nilavilakku lamp.",
"- **Temple or church architecture:** wide frames that show the setting.",
"- **Family spreads:** both families clearly arranged.",
"- **Sadya spread:** the traditional feast is a favourite for many families.",
"## Typography",
"Elegant serif fonts and simple scripts suit Kerala albums. For Malayalam text, use a proper Unicode Malayalam font and ask a fluent person to proofread.",
"## Backgrounds and ornaments",
"Soft florals, subtle gold textures and minimal borders work well. Our [Kerala wedding album PSD collection](/kerala-wedding-album-psd/) gathers minimal, floral and classic designs suitable for this style. Use Hue/Saturation adjustment layers to turn bright ornaments into muted gold and cream.",
"## Photography considerations",
"Temple ceremonies may have photography restrictions, and lighting can be dim. Work with the photos you have; a few strong images in a clean layout look better than many weak ones. Correct colour carefully so cream and white fabrics look clean rather than yellow.",
"## Pre-wedding and reception",
"Kerala's backwaters, beaches and hill stations are popular pre-wedding locations. If included, give them a modern, airy section. Receptions can carry more colour and energy while keeping the same fonts.",
"## Final checks",
"Confirm names and spellings in both English and Malayalam, keep faces away from the fold, export in sRGB and get the couple's approval before printing. For the technical steps, follow [how to edit a wedding album PSD](/blog/how-to-edit-wedding-album-psd/)."]),
'telugu-wedding-album-design-ideas':('Telugu Wedding Album Design Ideas',[
"Telugu weddings are colourful and rich in ritual, often spread over several days with ceremonies such as Pellikuthuru and Pellikoduku, Mangala Snanam, Kashi Yatra, Jeelakarra Bellam, Mangalsutra Dharana and Talambralu. A well-designed album turns this sequence into a clear, grand story.",
"## Map the rituals",
"Customs vary between families and regions, so ask the family for the order of ceremonies and which ones they want emphasised. Use that order as the album's chapters. A typical structure might be:",
"- Opening spread with names and date.",
"- Pellikuthuru and Pellikoduku ceremonies.",
"- Mangala Snanam.",
"- Arrival, Kashi Yatra and the main ceremony.",
"- Jeelakarra Bellam, Mangalsutra Dharana and Talambralu.",
"- Saptapadi and blessings.",
"- Couple portraits.",
"- Family groups.",
"- Reception.",
"## Key moments deserve space",
"Jeelakarra Bellam and Talambralu are visually distinctive and emotionally important. Use sequence strips for Talambralu (the playful showering of rice) and large frames for the Jeelakarra Bellam moment. Keep these spreads clean so the action stands out.",
"## Colour and style",
"Telugu weddings are often grand and colourful: deep reds, maroons, gold, turmeric yellow and bright floral decor. Royal, golden and ornate layouts suit these ceremonies. Our [Telugu wedding album PSD collection](/telugu-wedding-album-psd/) focuses on royal, golden and ornate 12x36 designs. Even with grand styles, keep the area behind faces calm.",
"## Typography",
"Use a strong serif or decorative display font for event titles and names, with a clean text font for captions. For Telugu text, use a Unicode Telugu font and have it proofread by a fluent person; incorrect conjuncts are easy to miss.",
"## Family spreads",
"Large extended families are central to Telugu weddings. Plan dedicated family spreads for both sides and confirm the must-include groups in advance.",
"## Practical tips",
"- Rituals near fire and lamps create warm, mixed lighting; correct skin tones carefully.",
"- Keep the mangalsutra moment and faces away from the centre fold.",
"- Use one template family per event and recolour ornaments to match outfits.",
"- Alternate dense ritual spreads with single-portrait spreads for rhythm.",
"## Pre-wedding and reception",
"Many Telugu couples also have pre-wedding shoots and grand receptions. Use a lighter, modern style for the pre-wedding section and a glamorous, stage-focused style for the reception, keeping the same fonts throughout.",
"## Templates and workflow",
"Start with royal and golden layouts from the [Telugu wedding album collection](/telugu-wedding-album-psd/) or the [Karizma album PSD collection](/karizma-album-psd/). Follow our [wedding album layout rules](/blog/wedding-album-layout-rules/), and confirm all names, dates and spellings with the family before printing."]),
'tamil-wedding-album-page-order':('Tamil Wedding Album Page Order: A Practical Sequence',[
"Tamil weddings follow a sequence of ceremonies that families know well, so an album that follows the same order feels natural to them. This guide suggests a practical page order for a Tamil wedding album. Customs vary between families and communities, so treat it as a starting point and confirm the order with the couple.",
"## Before the wedding day",
"- **Opening spread:** the couple's best portrait, names and the wedding date.",
"- **Nichayathartham (engagement):** exchange of thamboolam, the bride's entry, blessings and family groups.",
"- **Pre-wedding shoot:** if included, a short modern section.",
"- **Pandha Kaal and preparations:** ritual preparations at home.",
"- **Mehendi or Nalangu:** playful, colourful spreads.",
"## The wedding day",
"- **Bride's and groom's preparations:** dressing, jewellery, flowers, family moments.",
"- **Vratham and Kashi Yatra:** where these are followed.",
"- **Maalai Maatral:** the exchange of garlands, often with playful lifting by relatives.",
"- **Oonjal:** the swing ceremony with pachai pidi rice balls.",
"- **Kanyadaanam:** the bride's father giving her hand.",
"- **Muhurtham and Thirumangalyam (thali tying):** the central moment, deserving its own large spread.",
"- **Saptapadi:** the seven steps.",
"- **Blessings and Ammi Midhithal / Arundhati darshan:** where followed.",
"## After the ceremony",
"- **Couple portraits.**",
"- **Family groups:** both families, with planned group spreads.",
"- **Reception:** entry, stage photos with guests, cake cutting if any, celebrations.",
"- **Details:** kolam, decor, the thali, jewellery, invitation, the feast.",
"- **Closing spread:** a quiet portrait or the couple leaving.",
"## How many sheets per section",
"Give the most sheets to the muhurtham and its rituals, then to family groups and the reception, because these are the pages families look at most. The Nichayathartham and preparations can be shorter. Write the plan as sheet numbers and get the couple's approval before designing. See [how many pages should a wedding album have](/blog/how-many-pages-in-a-wedding-album/) for planning help.",
"## Design style",
"Maroon, gold, temple green and turmeric yellow suit traditional Tamil albums, with motifs such as kolam patterns, temple gopurams and brass lamps used as accents. Our [Tamil wedding album PSD collection](/tamil-wedding-album-psd/) uses these styles at 12x36. Keep areas behind faces calm and use one template family per event.",
"## Text in Tamil",
"Event titles in Tamil (for example முகூர்த்தம்) add a personal touch. Use a proper Unicode Tamil font, check that all characters render correctly in Photoshop, and ask a fluent person to proofread.",
"## Final checks",
"Confirm spellings of names and family members, keep the thali tying away from the centre fold, export in sRGB and run the [print-ready checklist](/blog/print-ready-psd-checklist/) before sending files to the lab."]),
})
_ADD={
'christian-wedding-album-design':["## Covers and keepsakes","A white or ivory cover with a single portrait from the church steps, or a simple floral design with the couple's names, suits most Christian albums. Some couples also like a small separate album for parents with the ceremony and family groups only. Keep the same typography on both so they look like a set, and see the [album cover design guide](/blog/album-cover-design-guide/) for layout tips."],
'hindu-wedding-album-design':["## Multi-day weddings","When ceremonies happen over two or three days, photos often come from different lighting conditions and sometimes different photographers. Colour-correct each day as a group, and use a slightly different but related background family for each day so the album has chapters without losing consistency. A small event title on the first spread of each day helps families find their favourite moments quickly."],
'pre-wedding-album-ideas':["## Common pre-wedding mistakes","The most frequent problems are using traditional heavy ornaments on cinematic photos, mixing photos with different colour grades on one spread, and placing the couple exactly on the fold of a panoramic image. Another is including too many near-identical frames from the same pose; choose the single best one. A shorter album with only strong images almost always feels more premium than a long one padded with similar shots."],
'engagement-album-layouts':["## Planning the number of sheets","Count the strong photos for each part of the engagement before deciding the length. A short, focused album with one spread each for arrivals, rituals, the ring exchange, blessings, couple portraits, family and the celebration often works better than a long one. If the family wants every guest included, offer a guest spread or an online gallery rather than shrinking every photo."],
'kerala-wedding-album-design-ideas':["## Keeping it understated","The strength of a Kerala album is restraint. Limit each spread to one hero image and a few supporting photos, use the same cream or soft gold background family throughout the ceremony section and let the kasavu, jasmine and temple settings provide the colour. If a template feels too ornate, hide half its ornaments and lower the saturation of the rest."],
'telugu-wedding-album-design-ideas':["## Balancing grandeur and clarity","Grand templates can quickly become crowded when combined with colourful ritual photos. A useful approach is to keep ornate borders and gold textures for chapter-opening spreads and use simpler layouts with plainer backgrounds for dense ritual sequences. This keeps the album rich in style while making sure every face remains easy to see. Proof each spread at a small size, like a phone screen, to check that the main moment still stands out.","## Covers","A cover with a single portrait of the couple in their wedding outfits, names in a strong serif font and a subtle gold pattern suits most Telugu albums. Keep text inside the safe area and check spellings in English and Telugu."],
'tamil-wedding-album-page-order':["## Adapting the order","Not every family follows every ritual listed here, and the order can differ between communities and between families from different districts. Some weddings combine the engagement with the wedding day, some skip Kashi Yatra, and many add a separate reception day. Share the planned sequence with the couple as a simple list and adjust it before you start designing; it takes minutes and prevents rearranging finished spreads later. Elders in the family are usually the best people to confirm the sequence."],
}
